# Environment Variables Guide

## REQUIRED_CORE
These are essential for the application to boot.

- `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`: Your Supabase Project URL.
- `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`: Your Supabase Anon Key.
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`: Server-side secret for admin operations. (Private)

## OPTIONAL_PAYMENT
Required for automated Binance Pay integration. bKash/Nagad continue to work manually if these are missing.

- `BINANCE_PAY_API_KEY`: API Key from Binance Merchant Portal. (Private)
- `BINANCE_PAY_SECRET_KEY`: Secret Key from Binance Merchant Portal. (Private)
- `BINANCE_PAY_MERCHANT_ID`: Merchant ID from Binance Merchant Portal. (Private)
- `BINANCE_PAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`: Secret used to verify Binance webhooks. (Private)

## OPTIONAL_FULFILLMENT
Required for automated Eklas license generation.

- `EKLAS_LICENSE_API_KEY`: Production API Key for Eklas. (Private)

## OPTIONAL_EMAIL
Required for email notifications. Licenses remain available in the customer library if missing.

- `EMAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY`: Resend or SendGrid API Key. (Private)
- `SMTP_HOST`: SMTP Hostname.
- `SMTP_PORT`: SMTP Port.
- `SMTP_USER`: SMTP Username.
- `SMTP_PASS`: SMTP Password. (Private)
- `EMAIL_FROM`: The sender email address.

---
**Security Note:** Never prefix server-side secrets with `VITE_`.
Scan your repository regularly to ensure no `.env` files are tracked.
